WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.830
From its very first episode, Lost made no
attempt to hide its fondness for perplexing

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:06.360
mysteries.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:11.020
True to form, the series finale left audiences
absolutely baffled.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:15.879
So if you want to know what really happened
on that island, get ready for a deep dive

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:17.980
into the ending of Lost.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:23.020
For much of Lost's run, fans worried that
the show would end with a "they were dead

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:24.420
the whole time" twist.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:31.020
Creator J.J. Abrams and showrunners Damon
Lindelof and Carlton Cuse repeatedly denied

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:35.500
speculation that the characters died in the
crash and that the island was a form of purgatory.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:40.680
Nevertheless, some viewers thought the finale's
church-set ending confirmed that they had

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:45.480
been lying the whole time, and that the entire
show had taken place in the afterlife.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.480
This interpretation was also supported by
the footage of the original plane crash and

00:00:50.489 --> 00:00:54.870
empty beaches that aired over the closing
credits, which some fans thought meant there

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:56.360
had been no survivors.

00:00:56.550 --> 00:01:00.260
But it turns out that the crash footage at
the end was never meant to be considered part

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.540
of the finale proper.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:07.500
Instead, as an ABC spokesperson later explained,
it was included so that fans could, quote,

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.640
"decompress before heading into the news."

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:14.170
The network never imagined that viewers would
consider this part of the show's narrative.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:19.780
Furthermore, "The End" takes pains to explicitly
clarify that all the events that took place

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:22.040
on the island were, in fact, real.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:29.280
"The most important part of your life was
the time that you spent with these people."

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:35.600
After five seasons filled with flashbacks
and then flash-forwards, the first episode

00:01:35.609 --> 00:01:42.049
of season six included something Lost fans
were totally unprepared for: a flash-sideways,

00:01:42.049 --> 00:01:47.630
exploring an alternate reality in which Oceanic
Flight 815 doesn't crash, instead landing

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:49.260
safely at LAX.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:52.860
And that's not the only thing different about
the two realities.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:55.460
Instead of being a con man, Sawyer is a cop.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:02:00.300
Instead of the strained marriage they had
in the pilot, Jin and Sun are secret lovers.

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:05.340
And the childless Jack suddenly has a teenage
son whose mother is none other than Juliet,

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:06.980
a woman he met on the island.

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:08.360
Was this all a dream?

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:13.100
Or was it perhaps a parallel dimension created
by the wonky powers of the island?

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:18.520
Or was this the true timeline, and maybe the
island is just an elaborate "what if" scenario?

00:02:18.849 --> 00:02:24.500
In "The End," the flash-sideways is revealed
to be the afterlife, where all the Oceanic

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:27.410
survivors are brought back together following
their deaths.

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:32.280
In a way, it is a sort of purgatory where
they each have to make peace with the struggles

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:36.120
of their lives before they can recognize one
another and move on together.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:42.000
This is where the Lost finale tripped up many
of its viewers, who reasonably assumed that

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.930
in order for all of the characters on the
show to have arrived in the afterlife at the

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:48.420
same time, they must've died at the same time.

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:53.440
But as logical as this reasoning appears at
first glance, it doesn't hold up under close

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:53.940
scrutiny.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:58.980
Not only does it fail to explain the presence
of characters like Juliet and Ben, who weren't

00:02:58.989 --> 00:03:04.069
on board Oceanic 815, it also doesn't account
for all of the shared memories they recover

00:03:04.069 --> 00:03:05.900
once they recognize each other.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:10.440
After all, if they all died in the crash,
how would Kate remember delivering Claire's

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:14.200
baby, or how could Sayid recall falling in
love with Shannon?

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:19.239
The explanation given in "The End" is that
they all died at different times, some way

00:03:19.239 --> 00:03:23.769
back in season one, and others many years
after the end of season six.

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:25.900
But time works differently in the afterlife.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:30.060
To the characters, it feels as though they
all arrived around the same time, even if

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.460
their actual deaths were many decades apart.

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:37.380
The only thing they all had in common was
that none of the characters in the flash-sideways

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:39.000
died during the plane crash.

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:44.900
We would be here all day if we tried to list
every death that ever occurred on Lost, but

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:48.140
here's what we do know about the deaths of
the people in the church.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:52.160
Boone dies in season one, succumbing to his
injuries after a fall.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:57.380
Shannon dies early in season two after being
accidentally shot by Ana Lucia,

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:02.020
and Libby dies toward the end of the second
season after being shot by Michael.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:07.260
Charlie dies in season three, drowning after
warning Desmond that the boat outside is "not

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:08.080
Penny's boat."

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:10.900
Locke is strangled by Ben in season five.

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:15.820
Juliet dies at the beginning of season six
after falling down a shaft and detonating

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:16.320
a bomb.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:21.840
Sayid dies midway through season six saving
his friends from a bomb, and Sun and Jin die

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:25.960
later in the same episode, drowning together
in a sinking submarine.

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:31.820
And Jack dies at the end of the series finale,
after being stabbed by the Man in Black.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:35.600
Then there are all the deaths that are left
up to our imaginations.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:42.370
Kate, Rose, Bernard, Sawyer, Desmond, Penny,
and Claire all survive the finale, and presumably

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:44.740
die at some point in the years afterward.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:49.680
And as the new protectors of the island, Hurley
and Ben likely outlive the other survivors

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:54.100
by quite a bit, but at some point, they must
eventually die as well.

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:59.520
A significant portion of the finale focuses
on the question of who will fill Jacob's role

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:04.310
as the protector of the Heart of the Island,
which turns out to be a magical, glowing pool

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:05.660
at the island's center.

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:10.960
This is supposedly the source of all life,
death, and rebirth, and according to Jacob,

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:14.880
it's the cork holding back a malevolent force
that could destroy the world.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:20.540
In the finale, this is revealed to be a literal
cork, which Desmond pulls to drain the pool,

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:22.600
nearly getting everyone killed.

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:28.100
The Heart of the Island also emits a strong
electromagnetic field and can manipulate space

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:33.460
and time, as evidenced by the relocation of
the island and the time travel in earlier

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:33.960
episodes.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:40.140
It's also implied to have a form of consciousness,
or at least self-preservation, granting immortality

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:44.440
to the humans who are willing to take on the
responsibility of keeping it safe.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:49.130
While some of the earlier mysteries of Lost
were revealed to have at least moderately

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:54.330
plausible sci-fi explanations, the Heart of
the Island requires viewers to accept some

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:56.420
elements of the supernatural as well.

00:05:56.760 --> 00:06:01.510
No details are ever given about its origins,
but it's said that a piece of its light is

00:06:01.510 --> 00:06:05.640
inside every living thing, and if it goes
out, so do we.

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:06.860
"What's down there?"

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:11.520
"Life, death, rebirth.

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:15.820
It's the source, the heart of the island."

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:20.520
Throughout the series, it's revealed that
many of the characters have some sort of connection

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:24.680
before ever boarding the plane, implying that
they were always predestined to board the

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:27.660
same doomed flight and end up on the island
together.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:31.740
In the final season, we learn that Jacob has
been pulling strings for years.

00:06:32.110 --> 00:06:35.740
He travelled around the world in order to
bring a group of potential "candidates" to

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:40.660
the island, in the hopes of finding someone
capable of taking over for him as the island's

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:41.160
protector.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:45.160
He knew that his brother, the Man in Black,
was searching for a way to kill him and would

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:46.400
eventually succeed.

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:49.600
So Jacob sought to find a successor before
that happened.

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:52.080
Jacob chose people who reminded him of himself.

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:57.110
They were individuals who were alone and flawed,
and who'd come to depend on the island as

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:59.480
much as it would rely on them to keep it safe.

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:05.080
All of the Oceanic 815 survivors fit this
criteria, and as the series progressed and

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:09.410
Jacob was able to observe their interactions
on the island, he slowly whittled down his

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:10.640
list of candidates.

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:14.480
None of the connections we saw between the
characters were accidental.

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:16.580
They were all engineered by Jacob.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:23.300
One of Lost's most enduring mysteries is the
nature of the smoke monster, a seemingly sentient

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:27.620
column of black smoke that occasionally attacks
and even kills people on the island.

00:07:27.640 --> 00:07:32.380
It turns out that the smoke monster is another
form of the Man in Black, who transformed

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:36.680
when Jacob threw him into the Heart of the
Island after the Man in Black killed their

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:37.180
mother.

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:42.300
For the next 2000 years, Jacob and the Man
in Black oppose one another, as the Man in

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:47.140
Black searches for a way around the supernatural
law that keeps him from killing Jacob.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:54.540
"One of these days, sooner or later, I'm going
to find a loophole, my friend."

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:57.740
"Well, when you do, I'll be right here."

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:01.960
As the smoke monster, he can't be killed,
but he also can't leave.

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:06.820
Over the years, he assumes his smoke form
in order to kill the candidates Jacob brings

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:11.310
to the island, hoping that if Jacob dies and
leaves no successor, the Man in Black can

00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:12.220
finally leave.

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:17.180
Ultimately, though, the Man in Black's immortality
is linked to the Heart of the Island, so when

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:22.500
Desmond temporarily shuts it down in the finale,
he's made mortal and killed by Kate and Jack,

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:24.740
ending the smoke monster forever.

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:29.890
The DHARMA Initiative first came to the island
in the 1970s, with the objective of studying

00:08:29.890 --> 00:08:34.900
the island's unique properties and harnessing
them in the name of scientific advancement.

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:39.570
While DHARMA conducted research across all
fields, attempting to uncover the island's

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:43.340
secrets, they never fully understood what
they were dealing with when it came to the

00:08:43.340 --> 00:08:45.260
supernatural Heart of the Island.

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:49.520
But that didn't stop them from trying, and
they constructed stations all over the island

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:53.320
in an attempt to make sense of the bizarre
phenomena they were witnessing.

00:08:53.570 --> 00:08:58.060
DHARMA was eventually wiped out by a group
of people living on the island who were devoted

00:08:58.060 --> 00:09:02.680
to Jacob, known to the Oceanic 815 survivors
as "the Others."

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:07.680
By the time Oceanic 815 crashed, DHARMA was
long gone, leading the survivors to wonder

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:12.380
whether DHARMA might've been responsible for
some of the strange happenings on the island.

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:15.980
But DHARMA didn't create any of the island's
powers.

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:20.700
Those already existed long before the scientists
showed up, and were in fact the reason why

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:22.460
they came in the first place.

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:27.200
At the end of the finale, after the main characters
have regained their memories of their time

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:31.350
together on the island, they make their way
to a church, where they see the symbols of

00:09:31.350 --> 00:09:32.520
a number of different faiths.

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:37.580
Christian Shephard then explains to his son
Jack that the flash-sideways were constructed

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:41.150
by and for the Oceanic 815 survivors.

00:09:41.420 --> 00:09:46.300
"This is a place that you all made together
so that you could find one another."

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:51.260
According to Christian, once they were all
ready to do so, they each showed up at the

00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:52.480
church, one by one.

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:56.940
When Jack first arrives at the church, he
sees his father's coffin, and seems to think

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:58.260
he's there for his funeral.

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:03.010
But the coffin is empty, and the funeral that
he'd expected is replaced by a reunion with

00:10:03.010 --> 00:10:05.700
his loved ones and hope for a new future together.

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:09.700
The church seems to symbolize that all the
characters have said their goodbyes to their

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:13.180
past lives, and they're finally ready to be
at peace with one another.

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:17.680
When Christian opens the doors at the end
of the episode and light floods the church,

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:21.820
it's safe to assume that signifies "moving
on," whatever that means.

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:27.900
Even though Ben Linus's presence in the flash-sideways
seems to indicate that the Oceanic survivors

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:32.720
were the most significant people in his life,
he elects not to enter the church with them.

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:37.000
"You know, you were a real good number two."

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:41.160
"You were a great number one, Hugo."

00:10:42.260 --> 00:10:46.200
This exchange between Ben and Hurley seems
to indicate that they worked together on the

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:49.020
island for a long time after the events of
the finale.

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:53.940
That Ben was drawn to the church with the
rest of them may be an indication that, cosmically

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:58.450
at least, his service to the island was enough
to redeem him for the horrible things he'd

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:01.200
done in life, and that he could move on with
the others.

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:05.880
However, Ben opting not to enter the church
could mean that he isn't ready to move on

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:06.380
yet.

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:11.440
Perhaps he still has more people to find in
the afterlife before he can let go, or maybe,

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:15.570
despite having been forgiven by some of the
people he wronged, he still has to come to

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:17.060
terms with what he did.

00:11:17.140 --> 00:11:22.060
It's never clarified what happens to Ben after
he decides to stay outside, but we can only

00:11:22.060 --> 00:11:24.520
hope that, eventually, he finds peace.

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:29.420
And hopefully, after nearly a decade, all
of us can find peace with this show that deeply

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:31.220
affected so many of us!

